  "figure": {
    "caption": "Triangle counting [Chand2026Triangle] on a triangle: after dispersing (one agent per node), electing a leader and learning $\\Delta$ (not shown), the agents write their IDs in 2 bits. In block $i$ (of $2\\Delta = 4$ rounds) agents whose $i$-th bit is 1 walk to each neighbour and back, one edge per round, while the others wait. In the first pass a visit to a waiting neighbour records both IDs (green edges); in the second pass, round by round with the same walks, the two ends of each edge count the IDs on both lists (blue numbers). Each agent adds its edges' counts and halves the sum: the number of triangles at its node.",
